# RETRACTION AND VERDICT, both from the control arm.
#
# 1. THE 60-vs-120 REGRESSION I REPORTED FROM THE AUDIT IS WITHDRAWN.  Arm A here is the audit's
#    exact 120 s configuration, and the two runs disagree by more than the effect I claimed:
#
#        inst   audit A(120s)      ff120 A(120s)     apart
#        P13     68,679,956    ->   69,056,997       0.55%
#        P2      61,457,557    ->   59,827,452       2.65%
#        P36     79,484,298    ->   75,440,326       5.36%
#
#    The claimed regressions were +1.85 / +2.23 / +4.76 / +1.96.  Every one is inside the control's
#    own spread.  I also called P36 a zero-spread instance: that was measured at 60 s (lnshold,
#    two identical replicates) and does not transfer to 120 s, where it moves 5.36%.
#
#    This is the second time today I built a finding on single cells per side -- the -fopenmp
#    branch was the first, opened on two lucky cells and closed when the control was replicated.
#    The rule I already knew and did not apply: measure the control's spread before measuring the
#    effect.
#
# 2. ARM B IS REJECTED, and it is rejected by the pre-registered clause rather than by a mean.
#    B genuinely spends the time -- wall against arm A is +2.0 s on P13, +21.0 s on P2, +19.1 s on
#    P36, so the gate does open and the fill round does run -- and the objective does not follow:
#
#        P13  +0.00%   (byte-identical)      P2  -0.10%      P36  +2.74%
#
#    The clause fixed before the run was "an arm that extends the wall without improving the
#    objective has proved the time was worthless, which closes this branch".  P36 spends 19 extra
#    seconds and returns a WORSE answer.  The half of the diagnosis that held is that FILLFLOOR=40
#    was refusing rounds at 120 s; the half that failed is that those rounds were worth anything.
#
# 3. SAFETY NOTE, recorded even though the arm is dead: B reached wall 115.25 s against a 120 s
#    limit on P36, a 4.75 s margin.  Lowering FILLFLOOR trades wall margin, and overrun is
#    disqualification-class rather than score-class.
